## Erlang VM flags for the release (see `mix help release`).

## Dirty schedulers don't busy-wait. Every SQLite call is a dirty-IO NIF, so with the default
## spinning, idle dirty threads (10 IO + one CPU per core) keep the CPUs busy and slow the request
## processes down. Natively on 4 pinned CPUs this gives +6–13% at 16/64 clients on every DB route
## and about -4% at 1 client. Normal schedulers keep their default busy-wait: turning it off too
## measured no better natively and ~25% worse for posts under Docker Desktop (bench/PERF.md).
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
